;; What the model reads of what brainyard/discovery.clj's tools say back to it:
;; errors that say what to do next, notes, refusals (brainyard.tool-words/says,
;; byj-2e8.9). Read by the model, so a resource (RFC-001).
{"discovery/family-summary"
  "This is a summary. For a family's tools with their descriptions, call list-tools with :family (e.g. {:family \"config\"}); to find a tool by what it does, :pattern — a case-insensitive regex over ids and descriptions (e.g. {:pattern \"issue\"}). Then get-tool-info {:tool-id \"…\"} for the parameters of the one you will call."
 "discovery/detail-note"
  "with their parameters they do not fit in one result — ask for :detail with a :family or a :pattern that names fewer"}
